roguery","bad manners","badness","delinquency","devilishness","devilment","devilry","deviltry","disobedience","elfishness","goings-on","hanky-panky","impishness","impropriety","misbehavior","mischief","mischievousness","misconduct","misdemeanor","monkey business","naughtiness","prankishness","pranksomeness","puckishness","rascality","roguery","roguishness","scampishness","wrong","wrongness"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["in the wrong"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b2839b8507385f7c4f","definition":"To treat unjustly; to injure or harm; to do wrong by.","example":"The dealer wronged us by selling us this lemon of a car.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["in the wrong","wronged","wrung"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e0e7a3a0f926ed63bd","definition":"To deprive of some right, or to withhold some act of justice.","example":"... And might by no suit gain our audience. When we are wrong'd and would unfold our griefs, We are denied access unto his person Even by those men that most have done us wrong.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["in the wrong","wronged","wrung"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:71238d1a1e967b9578","definition":"To slander; to impute evil to unjustly.","example":"O masters! if I were dispos'd to stir Your hearts and minds to mutiny and rage, I should do Brutus wrong, and Cassius wrong, Who (you all know) are